  "notes": "Conjugates as a godan verb: {剥|は}がない, {剥|は}いで, {剥|は}いだ. The action is more forceful and rough compared to {剥|む}く (to peel gently, as with fruit).\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {剥|は}ぐ — to strip/tear off (forceful removal of a covering)\n- {剥|む}く — to peel (gentler; fruit, vegetables)\n- {剥|は}がす — to peel off, to remove (stickers, labels, tape)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {皮|かわ}を{剥|は}ぐ (to strip off skin/bark)\n- {服|ふく}を{剥|は}ぐ (to strip someone of clothes)\n- {仮面|かめん}を{剥|は}ぐ (to tear off a mask — also figurative)",
